    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\">Comparison of the anatomy and the demographic and clinicopathological characteristics of squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) of the pinna, external auditory canal, and middle ear <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{22342554; 18948828; 32366754; 33568243; 24121777}</span></p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Ruta Gupta",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Characteristic</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Pinna</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">External auditory canal</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Middle ear</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Anatomy</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">The visible outer part of the ear with skin covering cartilage</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Slightly curved canal, 26&nbsp;mm in length and 7&nbsp;mm in diameter extending from the pinna to the tympanic membrane; the external third is cartilaginous and the inner two&nbsp;thirds bony</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cavity containing three ossicles, internal to the tympanic membrane and external to the oval window</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Site of SCC</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Skin of the pinna</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Skin of the external auditory canal</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Metaplastic squamous epithelium of the middle ear</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Incidence</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Nearly 8810&nbsp;cases per 100&nbsp;000&nbsp;person-years</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Nearly 0.2&nbsp;cases per 100&nbsp;000&nbsp;person-years</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">0.017&nbsp;cases per 100&nbsp;000&nbsp;person-years</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">M:F&nbsp;ratio</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">9:1</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">1:1</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">1:1</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Age</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Seventh to eighth decade</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Sixth to seventh decade</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Sixth to seventh decade</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Risk factors</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Solar ultraviolet (UV) radiation damage in Fitzpatrick skin types&nbsp;1, 2, and&nbsp;3</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Frostbite</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Immunosuppression</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Chronic otitis externa</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Chronic suppurative otitis media</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Irradiation</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Rarely, malignant transformation of sinonasal-type papillomas</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Chronic otitis media</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Irradiation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Clinical presentation</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Ulceroproliferative lesion on the pinna</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Nonspecific symptoms of chronic otorrhoea, otalgia, bleeding, hearing loss, otitis externa or otitis media, and facial palsy</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Rarely, an ulcerated mass</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Nonspecific symptoms of chronic otorrhoea, otalgia, bleeding, conductive hearing loss, otitis media, vertigo, and facial palsy</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Late presentation due to the mass filling up the middle ear and the mastoid</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Histology</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Typical histological features of SCC, with polygonal cells with intracytoplasmic keratin and intercellular bridges</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Degree of keratinization, nuclear pleomorphism, and mitosis depends on the grade of SCC</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 378.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"505\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Most tumours are well to moderately differentiated, demonstrating typical features of keratinizing SCC</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Genetic alterations such as <em>DEK</em>::<em>AFF2</em> should be considered in poorly differentiated non-keratinizing SCC</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Viral etiology and genetic alterations should be considered for tumours extending from the nasopharynx or the sinonasal tract</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 9; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Immunohistochemistry</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Positive for cytokeratin, CK5/6, p40, and EMA</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 378.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"505\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Positive for cytokeratin, CK5/6, p40, and EMA</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Additional testing for EBER, NUT, CD99, and FLI1 should be considered in poorly differentiated non-keratinizing SCC</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 10; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Differential diagnosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Chondrodermatitis nodularis chronica helicis</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Basal cell carcinoma</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Melanoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Cholesteatoma</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Pseudoepitheliomatous hyperplasia</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Basal cell carcinoma</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Melanoma</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Extension of tumours from the parotid and middle ear</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Cholesteatoma</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Middle ear corpuscles</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Extension of tumours from the nasopharynx, salivary gland, and sinonasal tract</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 11; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Prognosis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Good prognosis after local resection</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Overall survival rate: 93&ndash;95%</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Risk of regional nodal metastases: 12&ndash;16%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Overall 5-year survival rate: 53% (88.4% for T1 and 26.8% for T4)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 189.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Poor prognosis due to advanced stage at presentation</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">5-year survival rate: 37% (range: 25&ndash;83%)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Death due to intracranial extension</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
